அடியுறை","parts":[{"text":"அடி","lemma":"aṭi","gloss":"feet"},{"text":"உறை","lemma":"uṟai","gloss":"dwelling/servant"}],"gloss":"servant at the feet"},{"surface":"எனினே","parts":[{"text":"எனின்","lemma":"eṉiṉ","gloss":"if you say"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"if you say"},{"surface":"மாண்ட","parts":[{"text":"மாண்ட","lemma":"மாண்ட","gloss":"glorious"}],"gloss":"glorious","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்புறு","parts":[{"text":"இன்பு","lemma":"iṉpu","gloss":"pleasure"},{"text":"உறு","lemma":"uṟu","gloss":"have"}],"gloss":"delightful"},{"surface":"பேடை","parts":[{"text":"பேடை","lemma":"pēṭai","gloss":"female bird"}],"gloss":"female mate"},{"surface":"அணியத்","parts":[{"text":"அணியத்","lemma":"அணியத்","gloss":"to wear"}],"gloss":"to wear","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"தன்","parts":[{"text":"தன்","lemma":"taṉ","gloss":"his own"}],"gloss":"his own"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அன்புறு","parts":[{"text":"அன்பு","lemma":"aṉpu","gloss":"love"},{"text":"உறு","lemma":"uṟu","gloss":"have"}],"gloss":"loving"},{"surface":"நன்கலம்","parts":[{"text":"நன்மை","lemma":"naṉmai","gloss":"goodness"},{"text":"கலம்","lemma":"kalam","gloss":"ornament"}],"gloss":"fine ornaments"},{"surface":"நல்குவன்","parts":[{"text":"நல்கு","lemma":"nalku","gloss":"give"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he will give"},{"surface":"நினக்கே","parts":[{"text":"நினக்கு","lemma":"niṉakku","gloss":"to you"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"to you indeed"}]}],"literal":"O male swan! O male swan! / The lord of victorious battles who protects his land, / like his bright face, / the crescent moon with joined tips shines with budding moonlight, / in this bewildering evening when we, helpless, grieve, / if you, having eaten the ayirai fish of the beautiful great ghat of Kumari, / are returning to the northern mountains, on your way, / if you land in the good Chola country, at Kozhi, / resting your short wings on the high-level mansions, / without being stopped at the gate, entering the palace, / if you say to our great king Killi, 'I am a servant of Picir Antai', / he will give you, for your glorious, / beloved female swan to wear, / his own precious ornaments of love.","translation":"O male swan, O male swan! In this bewildering evening, as we grieve in helpless sorrow, the crescent moon with its tips joined shines with budding light, like the bright face of our lord of victorious battles who protects his land. If, after feeding on the ayirai fish in the beautiful, great harbor of Kumari, you fly back to the northern mountains, and on your way descend upon Kozhi in the fertile Chola country, rest your short wings on the high mansions, and enter the palace without being stopped at the gate, and say to our great king Killi, 'I am a servant of Antai of great Picir,' he will surely give you, for your glorious, beloved mate to wear, his own precious ornaments of love.","modern":"ஆண் அன்னமே! ஆண் அன்னமே! போர்களில் வெற்றி பெற்றுத் தன் நாட்டைப் பாதுகாக்கும் தலைவனுடைய ஒளி பொருந்திய முகத்தைப் போல, இரு முனைகளும் கூடிய பிறைநிலா அரும்பும் ஒளியோடு விளங்கும் இந்த மயக்கத்தைத் தரும் மாலைப் பொழுதில், யாம் துணையின்றி வருந்துகிறோம். நீ குமரியின் அழகிய பெரிய துறையில் அயிரை மீன்களை உண்டு, வடக்கு நோக்கி இமயமலைக்குச் செல்வாயானால், வழியில் உள்ள சோழ நன்னாட்டின் உறையூரை அடைந்து, அங்குள்ள உயர்ந்த மாடங்களில் உனது சிறிய சிறகுகளை அசைத்து இளைப்பாறி, வாயிலில் யாரும் தடுக்காமல் அரண்மனைக்குள் புகுந்து, எம் பெரு வேந்தனாகிய கிள்ளியிடம், 'யான் பெருமைக்குரிய பிசிர் என்னும் ஊரைச் சேர்ந்த ஆந்தையின் அடியவன்' என்று கூறினால், அவன் உனது சிறந்த இன்பம் தரும் பெண் அன்னம் அணிந்து கொள்வதற்காக, அன்போடு கூடிய நல்ல அணிகலன்களை உனக்கு வழங்குவான்.","explanation":"The poet Picirāntaiyār addresses a male swan flying northwards from the southern Kumari (Kanyakumari) to the northern Himalayas. He describes his deep grief in the evening, comparing the crescent moon to the bright face of his beloved friend, King Kōpperuñcōḻaṉ (Killi) of Uraiyur (Kozhi). The poet asks the swan to stop at the Chola capital on its way, enter the palace freely, and introduce itself as a friend of Picirāntaiyār. He assures the swan that the generous king will reward it with precious ornaments for its female mate. This poem beautifully illustrates the deep, long-distance friendship between the poet and the king, set against the backdrop of the migratory path of birds.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,0.9],[0.9,1.47],[1.47,1.78],[1.78,2.19],[2.19,2.5],[2.5,2.9],[2.9,3.3],[3.3,4.4],[4.4,4.6],[4.6,5.05],[5.05,5.5],[5.5,5.8],[5.8,6.38],[6.38,6.96],[6.96,7.68],[7.68,8.4],[8.4,9.4],[9.4,9.6],[9.6,9.9],[9.9,10.5],[10.5,10.8],[10.8,11.4],[11.4,11.9],[11.9,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,13.25],[13.25,14.0],[14.0,14.3],[14.3,14.8],[14.8,15.7],[15.7,15.9],[15.9,16.3],[16.3,16.6],[17.64,17.99],[17.99,18.34],[18.34,18.54],[18.54,18.94],[18.94,19.34],[19.34,20.54],[20.54,20.84],[20.84,21.14],[21.14,21.54],[21.54,21.94],[21.94,22.94],[22.94,23.13],[23.13,23.4],[23.4,23.68],[23.68,24.24],[24.24,24.86],[24.86,25.68],[25.68,26.29],[26.29,26.91],[26.91,27.32],[27.32,28.14],[28.14,28.34],[28.34,28.64],[28.64,29.04],[29.04,29.62],[29.62,30.34],[30.34,31.14],[31.14,31.44]],"female":[[0.0,0.6],[0.6,1.0],[1.0,1.51],[1.51,1.9],[1.9,2.53],[2.53,3.0],[3.0,3.4],[3.4,4.0],[4.0,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,6.0],[6.0,6.6],[6.6,7.0],[7.0,7.9],[7.9,8.6],[8.6,9.1],[9.1,9.6],[9.6,10.7],[10.7,10.9],[10.9,11.1],[11.1,11.9],[11.9,12.3],[12.3,12.8],[12.8,13.3],[13.3,13.6],[13.6,13.8],[13.8,14.7],[14.7,15.6],[15.6,16.0],[16.0,16.4],[16.4,17.6],[17.6,17.9],[17.9,18.3],[18.3,18.5],[19.68,20.13],[20.13,20.32],[20.32,20.8],[20.8,21.28],[21.28,21.68],[21.68,23.18],[23.18,23.48],[23.48,23.78],[23.78,24.28],[24.28,24.68],[24.68,25.78],[25.78,26.08],[26.08,26.4],[26.4,26.73],[26.73,27.38],[27.38,28.38],[28.38,28.68],[28.68,28.98],[28.98,29.48],[29.48,29.98],[29.98,30.98],[30.98,31.18],[31.18,31.78],[31.78,32.18],[32.18,32.67],[32.67,33.28],[33.28,33.98],[33.98,34.38]]},"sync":[[["அன்ன","swan"]],[["சேவல்","male bird"]],[["அன்ன","swan"],["சேவல்","male bird"]],[["சேவல்","male bird"]],[["ஆடுகொள்","victorious"]],[["வென்றி","victory"]],[["அடுபோர்","killing battle"]],[["அண்ணல்","lord"]],[["நாடு","land"]],[["தலை","upon"]],[["அளிக்கும்","protecting"]],[["ஒண்முகம்","bright face"]],[["போல","like"]],[["கோடுகூடு","tips joined"]],[["மதியம்","moon"]],[["முகிழ்நிலா","budding moonlight"]],[["விளங்கும்","shining"]],[["மையல்","bewildering"]],[["மாலை","evening"]],[["யாம்","we"]],[["கையறுபு","being helpless"]],[["இனைய","while grieving"]],[["குமரிஅம்","beautiful Kumari"]],[["பெருந்துறை","great harbor"]],[["அயிரை","ayirai fish"]],[["மாந்தி","having eaten"]],[["வடமலை","northern mountain"]],[["பெயர்குவை","you return"]],[["ஆயின்","if"]],[["இடையது","on the way"]],[["சோழ","Chola"]],[["நல்","good"],["நாட்டு","of the country"]],[["படினே","if [you] alight"]],[["கோழி","Kōḻi (the Chola capital Uraiyūr)"]],[["உயர்","high"]],[["நிலை","level"]],[["மாடத்து","of the mansion"],["குறும்பறை","short wings"]],[["குறும்பறை","short wings"]],[["அசைஇ","having rested"]],[["வாயில்","gate"]],[["விடாது","without stopping"]],[["கோயில்","palace"]],[["புக்கு","having entered"]],[["எம்","our"]],[["பெருங்","great"]],[["கோக்","king"]],[["கிள்ளி","Killi"]],[["கேட்க","so that he hears"]],[["இரும்பிசிர்","great Picir"]],[["ஆந்தை","Antai"]],[["அடியுறை","servant at the feet"]],[["எனினே","if you say"]],[["மாண்ட","glorious"]],[["நின்","your"]],[["இன்புறு","delightful"]],[["பேடை","female mate"]],[["அணியத்","to wear"]],[["தன்","his own"]],[["அன்புறு","loving"]],[["நன்கலம்","fine ornaments"]],[["நல்குவன்","he will give"]],[["நினக்கே","to you indeed"]]]}